17592186420405 1077 "selection" 13194139534375 17592186045417 true] [17592186420405 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420401 13194139534375 17592186045417 true] [17592186420405 1079 #uuid "ed0ab4b8-5966-5883-ba7e-805d59df8d8f" 13194139534375 17592186045417 true] [17592186420406 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420405 13194139534375 17592186045417 true] [17592186420406 1069 "q-213229" 13194139534375 17592186045417 true] [17592186420406 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534375 17592186045417 true] [17592186420406 1071 "![](images/9c/9cddd6584fee52757b1c7a470a6eeffee3678d569e36025ca70c99e5543c71c2.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above represent a relation, defined on the set $A={\\alpha ,\\beta ,\\delta },$ that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive?" 13194139534375 17592186045417 true] [17592186420406 1072 #uuid "d5414df0-8556-5960-86b0-386e378b451e" 13194139534375 17592186045417 true] [17592186420406 1074 "A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is \n\n- *reflexive* if $(x,x)\\in R$ for all $x\\in A,$\n\n- *irreflexive* if $(x,x)\\notin R$ for all $x\\in A.$\n\nIf some pairs of the form $(x,x)$ belong to a relation and others do not, then the relation is neither reflexive nor irreflexive.\n\nSince $R$ must be neither reflective nor irreflexive, some of the points $(\\alpha ,\\alpha ),$ $(\\beta ,\\beta ),$ and $(\\delta ,\\delta )$ must be in $R,$ and others must not.\n\nThese ordered pairs correspond to the diagonal points on the plots, as shown below:\n\n![](images/7d/7d4257c9e249f9a4c2a53c5566292e21ae6dfa7f0e08e27042548da2d8e7e000.png)\n\n \n\nA plot corresponding to a relation that is neither reflexive nor irreflexive must contain some diagonal points, but not all of them. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534375 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-25029d74-6c31-52ad-8e40-faedc9e473db" 17592186420400 "answer-4d14ebfe-075c-5ad1-ac77-3e3c8fa226f9" 17592186420401 "answer-618e807a-28cb-599f-9e9f-ea6004064c9e" 17592186420402 "answer-b23e5cb8-be50-53e9-bf